        "original_id": "f74e02f4-1a62-5533-a2eb-12f55107837e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Peter Jackson\n- Organizations: Keele University\n- Roles: scholar, historian, Emeritus Professor of Medieval History, editor\n- Topics: Crusades, European-Mongol contacts, medieval Muslim India, Timurid and Safavid periods\n- Places: Newcastle-under-Lyme, Staffordshire, England\n- Products: The Cambridge History of Iran: The Timurid and Safavid Periods\n\nFacts:\n- Keele University was founded in 1949 as the University College of North Staffordshire.\n- Keele University was granted university status by Royal Charter in 1962.\n- Keele University is officially known as the University of Keele.\n- Keele University is a public research university located about 3 miles from Newcastle-under-Lyme, Staffordshire, England.\n- Peter Jackson is a scholar and historian specializing in the Crusades, especially contacts between Europeans and the Mongols and medieval Muslim India.\n- Peter Jackson is Emeritus Professor of Medieval History at Keele University.\n- Peter Jackson is the editor of The Cambridge History of Iran: The Timurid and Safavid Periods.",
